{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00802",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 9.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Mr Doherty? I'm Fidelma, I'll take your temperature and pulse first. Sit there. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.91,
      "end_seconds": 20.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Thank you. I have a painful right ear, and I can barely hear out of it. Since Sunday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 32.82,
      "end_seconds": 35.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Temperature 37.0, pulse 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.91,
      "end_seconds": 43.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Good morning, Mr Doherty. How did the ear start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.68,
      "end_seconds": 55.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "I swam in the sea on Saturday, and the water got in, and by Sunday it was blocked, then painful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.18,
      "end_seconds": 60.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "How would you describe the pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.72,
      "end_seconds": 73.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "A throbbing ache, severe when I touch the ear, or pull on it, or chew. It wakes me at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.42,
      "end_seconds": 76.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Any discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.06,
      "end_seconds": 84.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "A little clear fluid, yesterday. Today it's gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.74,
      "end_seconds": 88.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Any dizziness, or ringing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.51,
      "end_seconds": 91.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No. Neither."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.51,
      "end_seconds": 96.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.25,
      "end_seconds": 103.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Ciprofloxacin gave me a rash, years ago, so I avoid that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.42,
      "end_seconds": 111.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "That's useful. Any health conditions, like diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.22,
      "end_seconds": 116.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "No, nothing. I'm fit as a flea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 121.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Do you swim regularly, or use earbuds?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.87,
      "end_seconds": 131.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "I swim in the sea three times a week, and I use earphones to run."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.88,
      "end_seconds": 156.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Let me look in your ear. This may be uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.56,
      "end_seconds": 162.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Ow. Ow. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.5,
      "end_seconds": 174.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "The ear canal is swollen and red, with some debris, and pulling the ear is very painful. I can't see the eardrum properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 177.31,
      "end_seconds": 181.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Doctor, he flinched a lot. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.98,
      "end_seconds": 193.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "It's an infection of the ear canal, outer ear, we call it otitis externa, swimmer's ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.5,
      "end_seconds": 197.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Can you treat it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.92,
      "end_seconds": 210.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "Yes. I'm going to prescribe ear drops with an antibiotic and a steroid, three drops, three times a day, for seven days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.23,
      "end_seconds": 215.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "In the right ear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.37,
      "end_seconds": 226.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Yes. Lie on your side, put the drops in, and stay there for five minutes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.61,
      "end_seconds": 229.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.66,
      "end_seconds": 241.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.56,
      "text": "And I'd like you to take paracetamol for the pain, 1 gram, up to four times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.27,
      "end_seconds": 243.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.77,
      "end_seconds": 252.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Keep the ear dry, no swimming, no earphones, and don't poke anything in it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.32,
      "end_seconds": 257.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How long off swimming? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.58,
      "end_seconds": 263.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Until it's completely better, at least two weeks. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 264.81,
      "end_seconds": 273.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "I'll clean the ear gently, if you like, doctor, before he uses the drops. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.21,
      "end_seconds": 284.93,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "Please do, Fidelma. And if the swelling closes the canal, the nurse may put in a small wick. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.88,
      "end_seconds": 288.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.91,
      "end_seconds": 302.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "If the pain gets worse, you get a fever, swelling behind the ear, or dizziness, come back the same day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.3,
      "end_seconds": 308.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I will. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
